cff-version: 1.2.0
title: MiniDOAS.jl
message: >-
  If you use MiniDOAS.jl, please cite it and, above all, QDOAS, whose analysis it
  reproduces (see "references").
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sunandan
    family-names: Mahant
    email: sunandanmahant@outlook.com
version: 0.1.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: https://github.com/mahantsunandan/MiniDOAS.jl
keywords:
  - DOAS
  - differential optical absorption spectroscopy
  - MAX-DOAS
  - trace gases
  - remote sensing
  - Julia
abstract: >-
  Differential Optical Absorption Spectroscopy in Julia. MiniDOAS.jl reads and writes DOAS
  files (MFC STD spectra, references, cross sections, calibrations, QDOAS project files
  and QDOAS-layout NetCDF results), prepares cross sections (slit functions and
  convolution, I0 correction, Ring spectra, air/vacuum wavelengths, wavelength
  calibration against the solar spectrum), and fits spectra with QDOAS's optical-density
  algorithm, ported routine by routine so that the slant columns agree with QDOAS to
  floating-point precision, either from a QDOAS project or set up in Julia. It also
  computes solar positions and geometric air mass factors, fit-window maps and figures,
  and includes a command-line tool and a local web GUI.
references:
  - type: software
    title: QDOAS trace gas retrieval software
    version: 3.7.13
    authors:
      - family-names: Fayt
        given-names: Caroline
      - family-names: Danckaert
        given-names: Thomas
      - family-names: Van Roozendael
        given-names: Michel
      - family-names: Vlietinck
        given-names: Jonas
    publisher:
      name: Royal Belgian Institute for Space Aeronomy (BIRA-IASB)
    doi: 10.18758/oqvqk2j3
    repository-code: https://github.com/UVVIS-BIRA-IASB/qdoas
    license: BSD-3-Clause
